# Playtest output written into whichever project is open — sweeps and their
# evidence (journals, captures, results) are runtime artifacts, never sources,
# and must not leak in from an example project someone playtested locally.
.hearth/evidence/
.hearth/sweeps/
# Conversations and tester sessions are the user's own record of working in a
# folder. They are written into whichever project is open, which includes the
# example games in this repo the moment anyone opens one, and a transcript of
# someone's afternoon is not a source file.
#
# `**/` is load-bearing. A pattern with an interior slash is anchored to this
# file's own directory, so the `.hearth/evidence/` and `.hearth/sweeps/` rules
# above match only at the repo root, not inside an example project, which is
# the one place their comment says they are for.
**/.hearth/chats/
**/.hearth/tester/

# agent/automation scratch (never commit to the public repo)
.scratch-audit/
.hearth-tmp/
scratch/
# Internal SDD/agent workflow artifacts — root only, so example projects'
# own .claude/skills scaffolding stays tracked.
/.superpowers/
/docs/superpowers/
/.claude/
/.worktrees/
